# serprog client (flashrom's traffic): JEDEC ID, a 16-byte read at 0x000100,
# read status, write enable, read status. The flash lane's host answers with
# ID EF 40 15, image byte a = a mod 256 and the write enable latch it keeps.
# MISO stays low while the controller sends opcode and address.
mosi=9F,00,00,00 miso=00,EF,40,15
mosi=03,00,01,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00,00 miso=00,00,00,00,00,01,02,03,04,05,06,07,08,09,0A,0B,0C,0D,0E,0F
mosi=05,00 miso=00,00
mosi=06 miso=00
mosi=05,00 miso=00,02
